---
/**
 * PRIVACY POLICY BODY. SHARED BY BOTH APPS.
 *
 * /privacy is a DEPLOY GATE (CLAUDE.md gate 8): the footer links to it from
 * every page and it currently 404s. This is the page that closes it.
 *
 * WHY IT IS SHARED. The two sites are the same practice on two hostnames and
 * they handle data identically: static assets, no forms, no cookies, one
 * mailbox. Two hand written policies would drift, and a privacy policy that
 * contradicts itself across a referral path is worse than a plain one. Only
 * the hostname, the address and the controller line differ, so those are
 * props.
 *
 * EVERY CLAIM ON THIS PAGE IS TRUE OF THE BUILD AS SHIPPED, and each one is
 * checkable rather than reassuring:
 *   - No form exists on either site. Contact is mailto, ruled 2026-08-09.
 *   - No script of ours sets a cookie. There is no consent banner because
 *     there is nothing to consent to.
 *   - Cloudflare Web Analytics is enabled in the Cloudflare dashboard and
 *     injected at the edge. It is cookieless and does not fingerprint.
 *   - Instrument Sans is self hosted, so no font CDN sees a visitor request.
 *     That is a real privacy property of the build, not a boast.
 *   - The old D1 site-tracking table stopped receiving writes when the worker
 *     was retired. Historical rows are retained, which is why retention is
 *     stated rather than claimed to be zero.
 *
 * NO RESPONSE WINDOW APPEARS HERE. Gate 2 covers copy as well as structured
 * data, and "we will get back to you within X" is the exact sentence it bans.
 * There is no sentence on this page about how fast anything is answered.
 *
 * NO EM DASHES AND NO EN DASHES. Checked.
 */
interface Props {
  /** Hostname as a visitor reads it, e.g. "clairvos.com". */
  domain: string;
  /** Legal controller, e.g. "Clairvos LLC". */
  entity: string;
  /** Controller address lines. */
  address: string[];
  /** The mailbox this site routes to. */
  email: string;
  /** Machine readable effective date, e.g. "2026-08-10". */
  effective: string;
}

const { domain, entity, address, email, effective } = Astro.props;

const effectiveLabel = new Intl.DateTimeFormat("en-GB", {
  day: "numeric",
  month: "long",
  year: "numeric",
  timeZone: "UTC",
}).format(new Date(`${effective}T00:00:00Z`));
---

<article class="doc">
  <header class="doc-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1 class="doc-title">What this site knows about you.</h1>
    <p class="doc-lede">
      Very little, and this page says exactly what. It applies to <strong>{domain}</strong>
      and to email sent to the address below.
    </p>
    <p class="doc-date">
      Effective <time datetime={effective}>{effectiveLabel}</time>
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="sec">
    <h2 class="sec-title">The short version</h2>
    <div class="sec-body">
      <p>
        This is a set of static files. There is no account to create, no form to
        submit, no comment box, and no login. Nothing on either site asks for a
        name, an address or a payment detail, so nothing collects one.
      </p>
      <p>
        No cookie is set by this site. There is no consent banner because there
        is nothing to consent to.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <h2 class="sec-title">Measurement</h2>
    <div class="sec-body">
      <p>
        Visits are counted with Cloudflare Web Analytics. It is cookieless, it
        does not fingerprint the browser, and it does not follow anyone between
        sites. What it reports is aggregate: which pages were viewed, which
        site a visitor arrived from, roughly where in the world the request came
        from, and what class of device it came from.
      </p>
      <p>
        None of that identifies a person, none of it is sold, and none of it
        feeds an advertising network.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <h2 class="sec-title">Hosting and server records</h2>
    <div class="sec-body">
      <p>
        The site is served by Cloudflare. Like any web server, Cloudflare
        processes the technical details a request has to carry in order to be
        answered at all: the IP address it came from, the browser it announced
        itself as, the address requested, and the time. Cloudflare acts as a
        processor here and uses that data to deliver the page and to block
        abuse. Retention is set by Cloudflare, not by this site.
      </p>
      <p>
        Fonts are self hosted, so no font provider ever sees a request from
        anyone reading this. There are no embedded videos, no social widgets,
        no advertising pixels and no third party scripts.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <h2 class="sec-title">Email</h2>
    <div class="sec-body">
      <p>
        The two contact routes in the footer open your own mail client with a
        subject already filled in. Nothing is sent anywhere until you press send
        in your own software.
      </p>
      <p>
        A message sent to <a class="link" href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> is
        stored in the mailbox it arrives in. The address, the message and
        anything attached to it are kept in order to reply and to keep an
        ordinary business record of the conversation. They are not added to a
        mailing list, not shared with a third party for marketing, and not sold.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <h2 class="sec-title">Historical records</h2>
    <div class="sec-body">
      <p>
        An earlier version of the engineering site logged referral information
        and contact form submissions to a database. That code has been retired
        and no longer receives anything. The rows it already wrote are retained
        rather than deleted, because deleting a record of a conversation someone
        started is not an improvement. They can be removed on request.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <h2 class="sec-title">Your rights</h2>
    <div class="sec-body">
      <p>
        Depending on where you live you may have a legal right to ask for a copy
        of the personal data held about you, to have it corrected, or to have it
        deleted. Ask by email and it will be handled.
      </p>
      <p>
        Since this site holds nothing beyond what is described above, in practice
        that means the contents of a mailbox and, if it applies to you, the
        historical rows in the paragraph above.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <h2 class="sec-title">Changes</h2>
    <div class="sec-body">
      <p>
        This page carries an effective date at the top. If what the site does
        with data changes, that date changes with it. There is no archive of
        earlier versions; the current text is the current practice.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <h2 class="sec-title">Who to contact</h2>
    <div class="sec-body">
      <p class="controller">
        {entity}<br />
        {address.map((line) => [line, <br />])}
        <a class="link" href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        {entity} is the data controller for {domain}.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</article>

<style>
  /*
    FIELD MANUAL REGISTER, A-D5. Numbered sections in mono down the left,
    prose on the right, hairlines between. The numbering is a CSS counter so
    it cannot drift out of sync with the sections, and a section inserted in
    the middle renumbers itself.

    No boxes, no cards, no rounded anything. A legal page is where the house
    style is easiest to abandon and is exactly where abandoning it shows.
  */

  .doc {
    counter-reset: sec;
    max-width: var(--max-w);
  }

  .doc-head {
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-label);
    font-size: var(--eyebrow-size);
    line-height: var(--lh-mono);
    letter-spacing: var(--eyebrow-track);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
    color: var(--fg-secondary);
  }

  .doc-title {
    margin-block-start: var(--s-4);
    font-size: var(--t-h1);
    line-height: var(--lh-tight);
    letter-spacing: var(--ls-display);
    font-weight: var(--fw-bold);
  }

  .doc-lede {
    margin-block-start: var(--s-8);
    font-size: var(--t-body-lg);
    line-height: var(--lh-body);
    color: var(--fg-secondary);
  }

  .doc-lede strong {
    font-weight: var(--fw-semibold);
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  .doc-date {
    margin-block-start: var(--s-6);
    font-family: var(--font-label);
    font-size: var(--t-mono-sm);
    line-height: var(--lh-mono);
    letter-spacing: var(--ls-mono);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--fg-secondary);
  }

  .sec {
    counter-increment: sec;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 18rem) minmax(0, var(--measure));
    gap: var(--gutter-wide);
    padding-block: var(--s-12);
    border-block-start: var(--hairline) solid var(--hairline-color);
  }

  .sec:first-of-type {
    margin-block-start: var(--s-24);
  }

  .sec-title {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-label);
    font-size: var(--t-mono-md);
    line-height: var(--lh-mono);
    letter-spacing: var(--ls-mono);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-weight: var(--fw-bold);
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  /* Mechanical numbering. FIG. 01 register, set at the size A-D5 asks for
     rather than at the size that feels tasteful.

     DELIBERATELY NOT INDIGO. Eight numbered sections would be eight indigo
     marks down one page, and "bold, purple and lines" is named in the grammar
     notes as the failure mode of a page whose only material is running text.
     There is zero indigo on this page. The rule is at most one moment per
     section, not at least one. */
  .sec-title::before {
    content: counter(sec, decimal-leading-zero);
    display: block;
    margin-block-end: var(--s-3);
    font-size: var(--t-h4);
    letter-spacing: var(--ls-heading);
    font-weight: var(--fw-bold);
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  .sec-body > p + p {
    margin-block-start: var(--s-6);
  }

  .sec-body p {
    color: var(--fg-secondary);
  }

  .controller {
    font-family: var(--font-label);
    font-size: var(--t-mono-md);
    line-height: var(--lh-body);
    letter-spacing: var(--ls-mono);
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  .link {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-block-end: var(--hairline) solid var(--hairline-color);
    padding-block-end: var(--s-1);
    transition: border-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out);
  }

  .link:hover,
  .link:focus-visible {
    border-block-end-color: var(--fg);
  }

  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .sec {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: var(--s-6);
      padding-block: var(--s-8);
    }
  }
</style>
